    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1114">

                <pb facs="1298" n="1102" xml:id="pg1102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/7–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1114<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Assistant to the Director of
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Director of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1114-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20">July 20 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. For Matthews from Reber.</p>
                <p>Please see Douglas’ telegram to
                        McCloy of today’s date.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1114-f2"/> He expresses personal regret to you and Clayton. I can not but share his views and
                    consider the situation would have to be completely reviewed in the light of what
                    appears to have been the decision to make no change until after the military
                    phase has terminated. We feel that it is important that some decision regarding
                    the future of the Commission after that date be made if possible during your
                    present conversations. As you know UNRRA’s
                    assumption of responsibility for supply to Italy, although still undetermined,
                    is nevertheless hoped for at an early date. We recognize this may preclude any
                    decision now.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1114-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1114-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Secretary of State at Babelsberg over the signature of Grew.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1114-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1114-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. Douglas declined the
                    prospective appointment.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
